<!--
  The Kaaba's hizam — the embroidered band round the kiswah — and its door, drawn on top of
  ic_kaaba.xml. The two viewports are identical and both are drawn into the same square, so
  the coordinates here are in the same frame as the silhouette's and must move with it.

  **Gold, since 15 Aug 2026, and the earlier decision not to use gold rested on an error.**
  This file used to be painted in the dial's face colour, and argued for it: gold "would be
  four more colour pairs to hold above WCAG AA", because the dial face is surfaceVariant
  normally and primaryContainer when you are facing the Qibla, each differing again between
  light and dark. That is true of anything drawn *on the dial* — and neither of these shapes
  is. Both sit entirely inside the wall (x 5..19 against a wall of exactly x 5..19), so the
  only pair that has ever needed to hold is this colour against the **silhouette's** colour:
  one pair per theme, not four. The old reasoning measured the wrong background.

  What the old choice cost is what the owner reported: painted in the page colour, the band
  is not a band, it is a *slot cut through the cube*, and a full-width slot near the top
  turns the strip above it into an awning. The mark read as a shopfront in both themes. It
  was never a contrast failure — both themes were already about 14:1 — which is why a
  contrast test could never have caught it and a screenshot did.

  Gold is also simply what is there. The hizam and the door are gold thread and gilded
  bronze on black cloth, and it is the one detail everyone recognises.

  Geometry, from the building: the hizam sits about two thirds of the way up (real: 9m of
  13.1m) and is roughly a metre deep, so y 9..10.2 here, leaving 5.5 units of cube above it
  rather than the old 4.5 — enough that the top can no longer read as a separate lintel. The
  door is 2.6 by 4.2, off-centre to the right as it is on the building, and it **stops 2.8
  units above the plinth**: the real door is raised about two metres off the ground, and that
  gap is most of what separates this from a box with a stripe across it.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FF000000"
        android:pathData="M5,9h14v1.2h-14z M12.8,13h2.6v4.2h-2.6z" />
</vector>
